==============================================================================
THREE NUMBERS PER ESTIMATOR: FLOOR, SEPARATION, EXPRESSIVENESS
==============================================================================
floor      = 95th percentile of |E(A) - E(B)| / E(A) across resamples,
             for the two arms the bench declares byte-identical, in percent
separated  = arm pairs whose 95% bootstrap interval for the difference
             excludes zero, over the arms that genuinely differ
sections   = exact count reachable by a strictly positive weighting on
             {median, candidate}; 1 means the candidate adds nothing

  bitpack-carrier-width   arms=5 regions=6 pairs=60
    estimator            floor %    separated  sections
    median                  1.16     57 of 60          1
    mean                    1.45     59 of 60          1
    iqr  (spread)          48.28     43 of 60          6
    idr  (spread)          52.15     47 of 60          7
    mad  (spread)          60.81     37 of 60          8
    p95  (level)            5.66     54 of 60          1
    p99  (level)            7.36     54 of 60          1
    p95-med (excess)      101.18     38 of 60          3
    p99-med (excess)      149.05     39 of 60          2
    correlation between separation and sections, over the 9 candidates: -0.641

